  "description": "BDD-style specification testing for xUnit v3. Provides [XF] (ExclusiveFact) attribute that prevents inherited tests from running in child classes, enabling nested class hierarchies that read like executable specifications without test explosion.",
  "iconFile": "compze-icon.png",
  "id": "Compze.xUnitBDD",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-25T02:53:02.173Z",
  "licenseExpression": "Apache-2.0",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/Apache-2.0",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "CvLMqbLfrwqOs9HnrzsQqI8vPscbRJkka/fO82qPBOvFNZO3HFTlpTx7eM+pzZK2SS+VhLw6PnzGpdWYYQB8dQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 58261,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/mlidbom/Compze",
  "published": "2026-11-25T02:48:29.487Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- **An `[XF]` declared on an abstract class fails, instead of silently never running:** an `[XF]` runs only in the class that declares it, and xUnit never runs an abstract class, so such a fact ran in no class at all, and nothing said so. Now each class derived from the abstract class lists the fact as a test that fails, saying to make it a `[Fact]`, which runs in every derived class.\n  - **What a consumer could notice:** facts that never ran now fail, once in each derived class, until each is made a `[Fact]` or moved to a class that isn't abstract.",
